# The `CET` zone and the `C-Eur` rules it used, extracted verbatim from IANA
# tzdata's "europe" file. Through tzdata 2020a, "europe" defined `CET` as its
# own standalone zone line (`Zone CET  1:00 C-Eur CE%sT`) with no LMT prefix,
# applying the `C-Eur` rule from time immemorial. Starting with a later
# release, upstream turned `CET`/`MET`/`WET`/`EET` into plain links (e.g.
# `Link Europe/Brussels CET` in "backward") instead of standalone zone lines,
# so a real-world zone that "starts with a named rule" (no earlier fixed
# offset period) is no longer available in current tzdata. This fixture keeps
# that shape locally so PeriodBuilder's handling of it stays covered.

